  "name": "Ink",
  "description": "Ink washed onto sized paper. Light: warm rice-paper ground, dense ink black type, and a deepened zhu-sha vermilion seal for the single accent. Dark: the wash inverted — the ink becomes the ground and the paper becomes the light, so form still carries the image. Shadows never take an offset, only wide diffusion, so depth reads as ink bleeding outward through the sheet rather than as a cast shadow.",
